Third-party licenses (vendor/)

CloudConnect ships a small set of Composer dependencies under vendor/,
needed for the Dropbox OAuth2 flow. All of them are MIT-licensed; the full
license text for each is included in its own vendor/<package>/LICENSE file.
Summary:

- league/oauth2-client
  Copyright (c) 2013-2023 Alex Bilbie <hello@alexbilbie.com>
  MIT License

- guzzlehttp/guzzle
  Copyright (c) 2011 Michael Dowling <mtdowling@gmail.com>
  MIT License

- guzzlehttp/promises
  Copyright (c) 2015 Michael Dowling <mtdowling@gmail.com>
  MIT License

- guzzlehttp/psr7
  Copyright (c) 2015 Michael Dowling <mtdowling@gmail.com>
  MIT License

- psr/http-client
  Copyright (c) 2017 PHP Framework Interoperability Group
  MIT License

- psr/http-factory
  Copyright (c) 2018 PHP-FIG
  MIT License

- ralouphie/getallheaders
  Copyright (c) 2014 Ralph Khattar
  MIT License

- symfony/polyfill-php80
  Copyright (c) 2020-present Fabien Potencier <fabien@symfony.com>
  MIT License

Two further transitive dependencies of the packages above (psr/http-message,
symfony/deprecation-contracts) are deliberately NOT vendored here, since
REDAXO core already ships the identical versions itself (see DEV.md,
"Keine Duplikate zu bereits von REDAXO-Core mitgebrachten Paketen").
